{"name":"Ephemeral Mist","hex":"#c7cdd3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ephemeral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lasting for a short period of time.","Existing for only one day, as with some flowers, insects, and diseases."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something which lasts for a short period of time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ephemeral"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ephemerality","blocks":[{"text":"Ephemerality is the concept of things being transitory, existing only briefly. Academically, the term ephemeral constitutionally describes a diverse assortment of things and experiences, from digital media to types of ponds and streams.\nWith respect to unique performances, for example, it has been noted that \"[e]phemerality is a quality caused by the ebb and flow of the crowd's concentration on the performance and a reflection of the nostalgic character of specific performances\". Because different people may value the passage of time differently, ephemerality may be a relative, perceptual concept: \"In brief, what is short-lived may not be the object itself, but the attention we afford it\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/MawsonPlateau-04.jpg/330px-MawsonPlateau-04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ephemerality"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Temple_Burn_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Temple_Burn_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Temple_Burn_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Temple_Burn_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Temple_Burn_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Temple_Burn_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The travelling festival Burning Man was described by one scholar as the \"very definition of ephemerality\".[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATemple_Burn_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/2006-05-20_-_Staircase_Falls.jpg/500px-2006-05-20_-_Staircase_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/2006-05-20_-_Staircase_Falls.jpg/1280px-2006-05-20_-_Staircase_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/2006-05-20_-_Staircase_Falls.jpg/500px-2006-05-20_-_Staircase_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Staircase Falls in Yosemite National Park only flows after heavy rainfall or snowmelt","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2006-05-20_-_Staircase_Falls.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/LakeBadwater.JPG/500px-LakeBadwater.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/LakeBadwater.JPG/1280px-LakeBadwater.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/LakeBadwater.JPG/500px-LakeBadwater.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lake formed at Badwater within Death Valley National Park during the unusually wet winter and spring of 2005","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALakeBadwater.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/WTC_smoking_on_9-11.jpeg/500px-WTC_smoking_on_9-11.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/WTC_smoking_on_9-11.jpeg/1280px-WTC_smoking_on_9-11.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/WTC_smoking_on_9-11.jpeg/500px-WTC_smoking_on_9-11.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Art Spiegelman, in reference to the September 11 attacks, described the World Trade Center as “ephemeral as...old newspapers”.[108]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWTC_smoking_on_9-11.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Sklen%C4%9Bn%C3%A1_plastika_d%C3%ADvky_s_anforou.JPG/500px-Sklen%C4%9Bn%C3%A1_plastika_d%C3%ADvky_s_anforou.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thum